  achieved/d1 near 1 means the walk is saturating its degree-1 ceiling and
  the session's low scores were the TARGET's fault, not the circuit's.
  Well below 1 means real headroom exists at degree 1 - which none of the
  nine interventions found, and which would be worth chasing.
  ceil d2 well above ceil d1 prices the pairwise upgrade for SET marking,
  a different question from the point marking that v42/v42b/v43 tested.
